We need to produce SHACL shape(s) implementing the supplied requirement: For ships operating where ice accretion likely, means to prevent ice accumulation on antennas required for navigation and communication shall be provided.

We have ontology terms: navigationOrCommunicationAntenna class, ship class, property antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent (datatype boolean) domain navigationOrCommunicationAntenna, property iceAccumulationPreventionMeansPresent (boolean) domain benchmarkEntity (but unresolved ownership). Also requiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna property string domain benchmarkEntity (maybe indicates requirement type). Also iceAccretionLikely boolean domain benchmarkEntity (but term owner is ship). termOwners mapping says iceAccretionLikely owned by ship. antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent owned by navigationOrCommunicationAntenna. hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna object property domain ship range navigationOrCommunicationAntenna.

We need to enforce that for a ship that has iceAccretionLikely true, all its required navigation/communication antennas must have antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent true? Or at least there exists means to prevent accumulation. The requirement: means shall be provided. Could be a property that indicates presence. So shape: for nodes of type ship with iceAccretionLikely true, then there must be at least one navigationOrCommunicationAntenna linked via hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna that has antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent true. Or could be all such antennas.

Interpretation: "means to prevent the accumulation of ice on antennas required for navigation and communication shall be provided." So each required antenna must have prevention means. So shape: ship with iceAccretionLikely true -> for each required antenna (via hasRequired...), the antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent must be true.

Implement SHACL: define shapes for ship, navigationOrCommunicationAntenna.

We need to use exact IRIs. Use sh:NodeShape, sh:property with sh:path, sh:node etc.

Define prefix: sh, xsd, rdf, rdfs, ex? but we can use full IRIs.

Target of ship shape: we have no specific target class defined? According to policy, we should not invent target selectors. The caller admission includes population of ship instances (synthetic). The shape may be activated with sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> maybe acceptable? But policy says do not invent missing owner bindings, applicability, etc. TargetClass is not missing; it's a class in ontology. It's fine to target class.

Thus produce shape:

<ShipIceAccretionShape> a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>; sh:property [ sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceAccretionLikely>; sh:hasValue true; sh:message "Ice accretion likely must be true for applicability." ]; sh:rule maybe use sh:node? Actually we need conditional: if iceAccretionLikely true then check antennas. Use sh:if with sh:target? SHACL doesn't have native conditional but can use sh:property with sh:path to navigate and sh:qualifiedValueShape and sh:qualifiedMinCount. Approach: use qualified value shape on property hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna to ensure each related antenna has antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent true.

Define shape for ship:

sh:property [
    sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna>;
    sh:node [
        a sh:NodeShape;
        sh:property [
            sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent>;
            sh:hasValue true;
            sh:message "Required antenna must have ice accumulation prevention means."
        ]
    ];
    sh:message "All required navigation or communication antennas must have ice accumulation prevention."
].

But we only want this when iceAccretionLikely true. To condition, could use sh:property with sh:ignore? Not in SHACL. Could use sh:targetClass ship and then a sh:rule with sh:if to add? SPARQL-based? Use sh:sparql where we assert violation when ship has iceAccretionLikely true and exists a required antenna lacking the prevention.

We'll implement a sh:SPARQLConstraint.

Create shape ShipIceAccretionPreventionShape with targetClass ship, and sh:sparql containing ASK to detect violations.

Example:

sh:rule not needed; constraint:

sh:property not needed, but use sh:sparql with select result set includes ?ship where condition.

Constraint:

SELECT ?ship ?antenna WHERE {
  ?ship a <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> ;
        <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceAccretionLikely> true ;
        <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasRequiredNavigationOrCommunicationAntenna> ?antenna .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?antenna <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#antennaIceAccumulationPreventionPresent> true .
  }
}

Then sh:message.

